 "description": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 18px; line-height: 21.5999984741211px;\">Fyllas Banke 3&nbsp;at 63&deg;55&nbsp;N - 55&deg;07&nbsp;W&nbsp;is a standard hydrographic station&nbsp;on the&nbsp;Fyllas Banke&nbsp;section and&nbsp;part of the Greenland Institute of Natural Resources monitoring program. The purpose of the marine monitoring program is to register specific&nbsp;physical properties&nbsp;of the sea water column,&nbsp;such as temperature and&nbsp;salinity,&nbsp;at the same geographical location&nbsp;once every year, and compare these repeated registrations&nbsp;with&nbsp;previous years&#39; recordings. Hydrographic measurements are&nbsp;typical carried out with a so-called &quot;CTD&quot; instrument (Conductivity, Temperature, and Depth). The hydrographic station is&nbsp;monitored one time each year&nbsp;in June/July.</span></p>",
